set heading(numbering: none)

`circle` · enclose · a closed or restricted version.

# Form

`x.circle` on a symbol, `(a + b).circle` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `sum.circle` | $sum.circle$ | built and cached |
| `plus.circle` | $plus.circle$ | font glyph U+2295 |
| `integral.circle` | $integral.circle$ | font glyph U+222E |
| `nabla.circle` | $nabla.circle$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A closed or restricted version. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A shape around the base: a circle, a box or a square. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.

# From LaTeX

`\oint` becomes `integral.circle`, `\oplus` becomes `plus.circle`.

